##### *Summary Table - Test Set Final Model Performance (XGBoost)*



```{r}
# Model name
testname <- c("XGBoost")

# ROC-AUC
testroc <- c(auc(xgbtestroc))

# Accuracy
testaccuracy <- c(xgbtestcm$overall["Accuracy"])

# Kappa
testkappa <- c(xgbtestcm$overall["Kappa"])

# Sensitivity
testsensitivity <- c(xgbtestcm$byClass["Sensitivity"])

# Specificity
testspecificity <- c(xgbtestcm$byClass["Specificity"])

# Positive predictive value
testpospred <- c( xgbtestcm$byClass["Pos Pred Value"])

# Negative predictive value
testnegpred <- c(xgbtestcm$byClass["Neg Pred Value"])

# Balanced Accuracy
testbalancedaccuracy <- c(xgbtestcm$byClass["Balanced Accuracy"])

# Summary table
testsummary <- tibble(Model = testname, ROC = testroc, 
                            Accuracy = testaccuracy, Kappa = testkappa,
                            Sensitivity = testsensitivity, 
                            Specificity = testspecificity, 
                            Pos_Pred_Value = testpospred, 
                            Neg_Pred_Value = testnegpred, 
                            Balanced_Accuracy = testbalancedaccuracy)


testsummary |> gt() |> fmt_number(columns = where(is.numeric), decimals = 3)
```



##### *Final Model ROC Curve Plot - Test Set (XGBoost)*



```{r}
plot(xgbtestroc, legacy.axes = TRUE,
     main = "Final Model ROC Curve - Test Set(XGBoost)", col = "darkorange", 
     xlim = c(0, 0.7), ylim = c(0.3, 1))
```



-   XGBoost was selected as the final model following its performance on the validation set compared with the other models.

-   Then evaluated on test set; The test results appear similar to the validation results, with high specificity but low sensitivity. Low sensitivity remains a concern.

